# GitHub Token for AI Models
# Get your token from: https://github.com/settings/tokens
# Required for automatic recipe extraction using GitHub Models (FREE!)
# Scopes needed: models:read (least-privilege for GitHub Models access)
#
# IMPORTANT: Both vars must be set with the same token value.
# GITHUB_TOKEN is used on native (via app.config.js -> Constants.expoConfig.extra)
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GITHUB_TOKEN is required for web builds (Expo only exposes EXPO_PUBLIC_ vars)
GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here
EXPO_PUBLIC_GITHUB_TOKEN=your_github_token_here

# Setup Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to .env (don't commit .env!)
# 2. Go to https://github.com/settings/tokens
# 3. Click "Generate new token (classic)"
# 4. Select scopes: models:read (minimum required for GitHub Models)
# 5. Copy the token and replace 'your_github_token_here' above (both lines)
# 6. Sign up for GitHub Models at https://github.com/marketplace/models (free)
# 7. Restart your development server (npm start)
#
# GitHub Models provides FREE access to GPT-4o, Llama, and other AI models!
